1.3.0: superjuice one-command file mode

superjuice INPUT.mp4 -c CAMERA [-o OUTPUT] now does the whole job:
drives FFmpeg for decoding and H.264 encoding (--crf, default 18),
passes audio through untouched, derives the output name as
INPUT_CAMERA.mp4, quotes paths safely for the shell, trims gate-crop
dimensions to even for yuv420p H.264, and reports missing ffmpeg with
the manual pipeline as the suggested fallback. Plumbing mode (y4m on
stdin/stdout) is unchanged for custom pipelines.

Movie tests gain file-mode coverage: output exists, video and audio
streams both present.
